WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
Give every project more depth,

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.800
texture, realism, and control.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.351
The Red Giant October 2026 release brings

00:00:06.351 --> 00:00:09.000
together five powerful updates for VFX artists,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.323
motion designers, and content creators,

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:13.840
each designed to make sophisticated visual effects

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.640
faster, more intuitive, and more art-directable.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.728
New in Red Giant 2027, Scene Light introduces

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:22.460
AI-powered depth-aware relighting directly

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.590
inside After Effects, helping artists place

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.620
lights into footage with natural fall-off

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.643
and scene interaction while keeping

00:00:28.643 --> 00:00:30.320
results fully in their hands.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.442
You can use it to integrate your VFX more

00:00:32.442 --> 00:00:33.474
realistically in a shot,

00:00:33.474 --> 00:00:34.720
create day-for-night effects,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.020
or just change the mood.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.322
For more on Scene Light, check out Chad's new

00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:40.060
tutorial on the Red Giant YouTube channel.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.780
One of our top feature requests is finally here!

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.459
Red Giant 2027 brings Cinema 4D's legendary

00:00:45.459 --> 00:00:48.200
procedural noise patterns into your timeline

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.540
or composite with Universe Maxon Noise.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.430
Now, creators with Red Giant or Universe subscription

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.680
can use these powerful GPU-accelerated tools

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.202
to build distinctive textures, animated maps,

00:00:58.202 --> 00:01:00.780
transitions, and abstract effects with amazing

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.860
detail and control.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.862
Learn more about Maxon Noise in Red

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:05.280
Giant with Chad's new tutorial.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.529
You can even use it for Real

00:01:06.529 --> 00:01:07.580
Lens Flares custom schmutz.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.340
That's right, you've asked and we've delivered.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.834
In this update, Real Lens Flares adds custom

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.140
schmutz textures for even more control over your

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.680
VFX and motion graphics.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.841
Plus, expanded light source types for

00:01:18.841 --> 00:01:20.960
even more realistic real-world lighting.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.179
For a deep dive into the new features in Real

00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:25.200
Lens Flares, check out Max's new tutorial

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.600
on the Red Giant YouTube channel.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.020
Chromatic displacement arrives in Autograph.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.844
With the organic prismatic distortion that you love,

00:01:31.844 --> 00:01:33.740
use it for force fields, refractions,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.100
heat ripples, transitions, and bold design work.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.088
Maxon Studio adds custom UI support

00:01:38.088 --> 00:01:40.000
so you can make advanced red giant...
